    "title": "Who's in Elite 8? Updated Women's March Madness bracket, NCAA Tournament schedule",
    "text": "March 27, 2026Updated March 28, 2026, 9:37 p.m. ETThe Women's NCAA Tournament's Sweet 16 is in the books.All four of the No. 1 seeds − UConn, UCLA, Texas and South Carolina − are still alive and looking to make their way back to the Final Four. The same group advanced last season, with UConn winning its record 12th national title under coach Geno Auriemma.Notre Dame, UConn, UCLA and Duke advanced to the Elite Eight on Friday night. Michigan, South Carolina, TCU and Texas joined them Saturday.Stay up to date with USA TODAY's team of journalists covering the women's NCAA Tournament throughout the 68-team dance. Keep up with all the results of the Sweet 16 here:Who's in women's Elite 8? Updated March Madness bracketNotre Dame (Regional 1 − Fort Worth)UConn (Regional 1 − Fort Worth)UCLA (Regional 2 − Sacramento)Duke (Regional 2 − Sacramento)Michigan (Regional 3 − Fort Worth)Texas (Regional 3 − Fort Worth)South Carolina (Regional 4 − Sacramento)TCU (Regional 4 − Sacramento)Elite Eight predictions: Who will advance to Final Four?USA TODAY Sports staff made their picks. Check them out here.Women's Sweet 16 schedule, March 27No. 6 Notre Dame 67, No. 2 Vanderbilt vs. 64 No. 1 UConn 63, No. 4 North Carolina 42No. 1 UCLA 80, No. 4 Minnesota 56No. 3 Duke 87 vs. No. 2 LSU 85Women's Sweet 16 schedule, March 28No. 2 Michigan 71, No. 3 Louisville 52 No. 1 Texas 76, No. 5 Kentucky 54No. 1 South Carolina 94, No. 4 Oklahoma 68No. 3 TCU 79, No. 10 Virginia 69Women's March Madness first-round and second-round resultsRegional 1 − Fort WorthUConn, Storrs, Connecticut | Gampel PavilionFirst roundNo. 1 UConn 90, No. 16 UTSA 52No. 9 Syracuse 72 No. 8 Iowa State 63Second roundNo. 1 UConn 98, No. 9 Syracuse 45Vanderbilt, Nashville, Tennessee | Memorial GymFirst roundNo. 2 Vanderbilt 102, No. 15 High Point 61No. 7 Illinois 66, No. 10 Colorado 57Second roundNo. 2 Vanderbilt 75, No. 7 Illinois 57Ohio State, Columbus, Ohio | Value Center ArenaFirst roundNo. 3 Ohio State 75, No. 14 How